<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>ort-server — Rust crate licenses</title>
    <style>
      body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 48rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
      .intro { background: #f6f8fa; border-left: 4px solid #d0d7de; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; }
      .license-text { background: #f6f8fa; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 0.85rem; }
      .used-by { columns: 2; font-size: 0.9rem; }
      h3 { border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding-bottom: 0.25rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Rust crate licenses</h1>
    <div class="intro">
      <p>
        These crates are statically linked into the <code>ort-server</code>
        binary through <code>third_party/tok_ffi</code>, the C ABI over the
        HuggingFace <code>tokenizers</code> crate. This file is generated from
        <code>Cargo.lock</code> by <code>cargo about</code>; do not edit it by
        hand.
      </p>
      <p>
        ONNX Runtime, cpp-httplib, nlohmann/json and Oniguruma are listed
        separately in <code>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code> and
        <code>licenses/</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Licenses used</h2>
    <ul>
      {{#each overview}}
      <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> — {{count}} crate(s)</li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>

    <h2>License texts</h2>
    {{#each licenses}}
    <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
    <h4>Used by</h4>
    <ul class="used-by">
      {{#each used_by}}
      <li>
        <a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">
          {{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}
        </a>
      </li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>
    <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
    {{/each}}
  </body>
</html>
